The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'bigquery-public-data': {'usda_nass_agriculture': ['census2012', 'census2012', 'census2002', 'census2007', 'crops', 'animals_products', 'census_2012', 'census_2012', 'census_2007', 'census_2002', 'environmental', 'economics', 'demographics']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• year – filter to 2022  
• group_desc – pick ‘FIELD CROPS’ for corn and ‘HORTICULTURE’ for mushrooms  
• commodity_desc – pick ‘CORN’ and ‘MUSHROOMS’  
• statisticcat_desc – filter to ‘PRODUCTION’ (the task explicitly asks for it)  
• agg_level_desc – filter to ‘STATE’ so we only keep state totals  
• unit_desc – must be ‘BU’ (bushels).  The requirement is explicit for corn and implicitly for mushrooms since the question says “measured in bushels.”  
• value – the numeric production figure we need; also require IS NOT NULL  
• state_name (or state_alpha) – identifies the state; will be our GROUP BY / SELECT field  
• table – bigquery‑public‑data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops (all queries use this table)

Typical WHERE block we will reuse  

WHERE year = 2022  
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'  
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'  
  AND value IS NOT NULL  

(plus the extra filters that narrow to corn / mushrooms / units / groups)

────────────────────────────────────────────
Ten exploratory‑to‑final queries
────────────────────────────────────────────

```sql
-- 1. Description: quick look at all production‑type commodities in 2022, 20 rows.
SELECT DISTINCT commodity_desc, group_desc, unit_desc
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: which measurement units are used for corn production in any year?
SELECT DISTINCT unit_desc
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE commodity_desc = 'CORN'
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
LIMIT 20;
```

